A||||6||85ZainoGT||I smell gas in my car or some odor||||8||
Z||000000||85ZainoGT||08-26-2001||10:32 PM||||ok ok, granted these cars arent coming right off the lot, they have been around for a while, im jus wondering if everyone experiences this... sometimes when I am driving my 85gt, I start to smell gas or like a smoke odor or something of that sort, you know what im talkin bout?  My car is a car that I REALLY want to take girls out with and stuff, but its not cool gettin out with a diff smell then you got in with, ya know?  anyone else get this?  anyone know how to take care of it?  thanks...||||reg||8
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||08-26-2001||10:37 PM||||Air freshner? hehe, check all your fuel lines under the car..and going up to the fuel rail..also my sharader valve was leaking because it didn't have a cap on it.<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: <B>KilleRedGT</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||08-26-2001||10:42 PM||||I guess that if you get out smellin like perfume or something else a little femine, that would be ok, but not hydrocarbons. Is it a gas/oil smell or more like antifreeze. Antifreeze could be indicative of a seeping heater core. Gas could be coming from fumes in the tank not getting captured by the evaporative cannister in the eng compartment. They can get plugged up especially if you routinely overfill your tank. There have been several discussions on both subjects. You can find em in archives.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leadfoot||08-26-2001||10:43 PM||||I would smell exhaust in my ride whenever the sunroof was cracked open.  I traced the odor to a leaking exhaust manifold you might want to start there.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||EdsB52||08-26-2001||10:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85ZainoGT:<BR><B>ok ok, granted these cars arent coming right off the lot, they have been around for a while, im jus wondering if everyone experiences this... sometimes when I am driving my 85gt, I start to smell gas or like a smoke odor or something of that sort, you know what im talkin bout?  My car is a car that I REALLY want to take girls out with and stuff, but its not cool gettin out with a diff smell then you got in with, ya know?  anyone else get this?  anyone know how to take care of it?  thanks...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"sometimes when I am driving my 85gt, I start to smell gas"<P>What did you eat for lunch?<P>"My car is a car that I REALLY want to take girls out with and stuff, but its not cool gettin out with a diff smell then you got in with, ya know?"<P>Depends; did you both enter the car together and leave with a different smell? Not always bad, just uncomfortable. <P>If it's gasoline, don't use heavy perfumes, just smells like a French whore. Seriously, I'd check all the good suggestions the previous posters recommended, and then check the gas tank seam if that's not it. Check the filler hose (can't buy 'em new anymore) whee it enters the tank at the aft end. I had a tank leak at the seam at the aft end once.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||08-27-2001||09:32 AM||||the filler pipe on my '85se leaked when I filled the tank up -had a pin hole that sprayed the gas onto the sound damping material in the side of the engine comparment<P>was leaking up under the wheel well - I had to pull the wheel well liner out and I fixed it with epoxy.<P>  if you got a gas leak you want to find it before some A.H. flicks a butt under your car someday.||||reg||10
Z||000006||Old Lar||08-27-2001||04:19 PM||||I had the cold start injector leaking gas.  Shut the car off, gas evaporates off warm engine. No liquid.  <P>The expert  looked at it and told me what it was, fixed it in 15 minutes.||||reg||1
